## Corrections

### Reply format after a push (user request, 2026-10-26)

The core file (section 2 and 11.7) says the reply after a push is the loader line and
nothing else. The user has since asked for a short fixed status block instead, so the
per-turn reply ends like this:

```
Skill updated: yes
- <what changed, one bullet per file or fact>
Hub Version: <e.g. v2.3>
Current Game Version: <the game script's VERSION, e.g. v1.4 (Ride A Dino)>
Hub loadstring: <the Hub one-liner with ?v=" .. tostring(os.time())>
GitHub: <https://github.com/bobashid/roblox-matcha/blob/main/File%20Name>
```

Rules that come with it:
- `Skill updated: no` when nothing was added to `SKILL Learned` this turn. Do not
  claim an update you did not push and read back.
- `Hub Version` is read from the Hub read-back this turn, never from memory.
- `Current Game Version` is the VERSION string of the script touched this turn. Omit
  the whole line when the turn touched no game script.
- The GitHub line is the blob URL (`/blob/main/`), spaces as `%20`, plus as `%2B`,
  same encoding rules as the raw URL.
- Every value must come from a tool result from this turn. If the Hub was not
  updated, `Hub Version` is the version read back, not a bumped number.
- This block replaces the "nothing else" rule for the reply body, but it does not
  replace read-back verification: no claimed version without a tool result.

Known conflict: core `SKILL.md` sections 2 and 11.7 still say the reply is the loader
and nothing else, and section 13 says the core wins on delivery rules. Until the core
is edited to match, say the block is per the user's 2026-10-26 request.
